  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">CLICK-IP2</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The two associations have decided to collaborate on developing common objectives, in particular those that support a world based onrelationships of solidarity and greater justice. The two associations agree that respect for Human Rights, including the Rights of Women and Children, forms part of their commitment, as well as respect for Social and Economic Rights for everyone. The Action that is subject to the present agreement is a contribution towards these objectives, but it cannot be considered as thesole link that unites the three associations.

The partner-CLICK and Oxfam-in-Laos undertake to build a relationship that reinforces each party&#x2019;s workand skills, while developing each organisation&#x2019;s respective strategies.

By way of an example, CLICKis interested in taking part inactivities that heighten awareness among the Laos public, by sending personnel and/or equipment in relation to the issue concerned by the Action. CLICK would also like to take part in the discussions held by the Oxfam in Laos on Strategic Reflections connected with the Action.
The two parties undertake to execute their activities with a view to achieving the following objective:

The overall aim of the project is Water Resource Governance (WRG) processes at the nationalare more inclusive of civil society, women and marginalised social groups.

And the specific objectives are:
&#x2022; To ensure social Inclusion, Gender Equality and Women&#x2019;s Leadership in Water Governance
&#x2022; To increase Civil Society Engagement and Networking at national and regional levels
&#x2022; To increase the voice of civil society and community in the development of hydropower and Sustainable Renewable Energy policy</narrative>
  </description>
  <participating-org role="4" type="72">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">CLICK Information for Development</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">CLICK is a local non-profit organization established since 2007 for promoting freedom of information and freedom of expression for development. Main activities include facilitating online repositories and discussion groups, community learning center, information clubs at colleges, social media, documentation of good practices, facilitation and documentation of learning events, media productions and networking of organizations.</narrative>
